AUDIO: 'Let\'s say we\'re working on an application that wants to present cloned AI voices to the user. Okay, we can connect our application to a texttospech server to generate that speech and then present it through our application. Great. But uh which texttospech engine should we support? There\'s a bunch to choose from. Okay, why don\'t we just'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'support all of them? Why don\'t we just allow the user to connect to any text to speech engine uh so that they have maximum flexibility? That\'s a great idea, but every texttospech engine supports a slightly different set of options and some TTS engines have options that are unique to that one'

[00:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'engine. uh how do we present that to our users in a way that isn\'t confusing? We can either support a lowest common denominator set of options that all of these TTS engines support, in which case we miss out on those unique features that some of them offer, or we present a'

[00:37] [scene:talk]
