[11:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'but not quite. I go I stop one level above that where I\'m just writing a detailed detailed spec and then handing that spec to the LLM and saying, "Okay, now you do it. I don\'t want to write the code. You do it." This is the best of both worlds. We have to be careful in'

[11:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'writing our spec. the spec has to be detailed enough for an LLM to work through. But LLM\'s love working through detailed specs. The more detail you give it, the better. And what I found was this technique that I\'m using, specri vibe coding. Uh I I come up with the spec and I I I give it to the LLM and I'

[12:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'say, "Don\'t write the code yet. What I want you to do is take a look at this spec doc and if I were to give it to you, would you be able to implement it uh in a in a reasonably competent way or is it vague or ambiguous?" And nine'

[12:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'times out of 10, the LLM will push back and say, "Well, no, it\'s this is this part. This part is vague. You said something in section one that is contradicted by something in section 4. You need to sort that out." And uh you didn\'t specify how this is going to'

[12:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'work, and you didn\'t account for this edge case. What if the data happens to go in this direction? All these different things. So, we we go back and forth with the document, tightening it up on every iteration until we\'ve got the document locked down tight. And then when the LLM has no more complaints,'

[12:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'then I give it to the LLM and the LLM just builds it for me. Uh that\'s great. So, my time is spent writing the docs that specify what I want done, and the LLM deals with the nitty-gritty details of actually implementing it. Now, this'

